Virat Kohli is an Indian international cricketer and the former all-format captain, widely regarded as one of the greatest batsmen in the history of the game. He is 37 years old as of December 27, 2025, born on November 5, 1988, in Delhi, India. 
Kohli retired from Test cricket in May 2025 but continues to play in ODI and T20 formats, recently becoming the second Indian batter after Sachin Tendulkar to cross the 16,000-run mark in List A cricket. 
